  "question": {
    "text": "The rate of a reaction A doubles on increasing the temperature from<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>310</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. By how much, the temperature of reaction B should be increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> so that rate doubles if activation energy of the reaction B is twice to that of reaction A."
  },
